**Read:** [Mesoscale tensile blind predictions — AM-Bench 2022](../sources/Mesoscale-Tensile-Blind-Predictions-AM-Bench.lingua#r_72TG9WD15YP5DCTVCCX26W7FND), challenge design and full results; [Manufacturing history and measured residual strain — AM-Bench 2018](../sources/Additive-Manufacturing-Residual-Strain-AM-Bench.lingua#r_1JF3D3C7YNFKCJET729ADPZWPM), announced and final measurement protocols.

A useful prediction states its inputs, output, conditions and comparison before observing the answer. A previously published dataset cannot become historically blind merely because the learner has not opened its final columns; it can still support a deliberately held-out educational exercise. Keep that distinction clear.

Test several observables and conditions related to the intended use. A model that matches global force may misplace local strain or failure. Different discrepancies can expose different missing mechanisms. Comparison needs uncertainty and a physical consequence of error; a league table alone explains little.

**Work:** Reconstruct what was genuinely available to the AM-Bench participants. Design a held-out exercise with an explicit record of which answers were hidden during model development. Compare at least two model choices across global and local responses. Identify a changed geometry, orientation or history that would be more discriminating than another repeat of the fitted case.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
